          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Telugu for to stress, then the Telugu for to bring up."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: మూలం",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "మూలం — mūlaṁ — \"a source; an origin\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ఆ వార్తకు మూలం ఏమిటి? ā vārtaku mūlaṁ ēmiṭi? What is the source of that news?"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "First a root: మూల కారణం is the root cause."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "మూలం (mūlaṁ) is borrowed from Sanskrit mūla, \"a root\" (CDIAL 10250); in Telugu it is the root of anything, its source or origin."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for giving reasons and opinions."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
