          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "దారితీయు — dāritīyu — \"to lead to; to result in\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "చిన్న అభిప్రాయభేదం పెద్ద గొడవకు దారితీసింది. cinna abhiprāyabhēdaṁ pedda goḍavaku dāritīsindi. A small difference of opinion led to a big quarrel."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (it …): దారితీసింది, dāritīsindi."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What it leads to takes -కి: గొడవకు దారితీయు (dāritīyu). Word for word, to take the road. Events lead to things, so its past is shown as దారితీసింది, it led to."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "దారితీయు (dāritīyu) is native Dravidian, a compound of dāri, \"a way, a road\" (DEDR 3170), and tīyu, \"to take, to draw\" (DEDR 3407)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
