            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "తలెత్తు — talettu — \"to crop up; to surface\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "కొత్త ఇంట్లో చాలా సమస్యలు తలెత్తాయి. kotta iṇṭlō cālā samasyalu talettāyi. A lot of problems cropped up in the new house."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (it …): తలెత్తింది, talettindi."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "తల, the head, + ఎత్తు, to raise: a problem raises its head. In this sense things crop up, not people, so its past is shown as తలెత్తింది, it cropped up."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "తలెత్తు (talettu) is native Dravidian, a compound of tala, \"the head\" (DEDR 3103), and ettu, \"to lift, to raise\" (DEDR 796)."
            }
          ]
        },
